rts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"மா","gloss":"great"},{"text":"கிணை","lemma":"கிணை","gloss":"kinai drum"}],"gloss":"great kinai drum"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கண்ணகத்து","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"drumhead"},{"text":"அகத்து","lemma":"அகம்","gloss":"inside"}],"gloss":"inside the drumhead"},{"surface":"யாத்த","parts":[{"text":"யாத்த","lemma":"யா","gloss":"tied"}],"gloss":"tied"},{"surface":"நுண்","parts":[{"text":"நுண்","lemma":"நுண்","gloss":"fine"}],"gloss":"fine"},{"surface":"அரி","parts":[{"text":"அரி","lemma":"அரி","gloss":"rattling pebbles"}],"gloss":"rattling pebbles"},{"surface":"சிறுகோல்","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"},{"text":"கோல்","lemma":"கோல்","gloss":"stick"}],"gloss":"small stick"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எறிதொறும்","parts":[{"text":"எறி","lemma":"எறி","gloss":"strike"},{"text":"தொறும்","lemma":"தொறும்","gloss":"every time"}],"gloss":"every time it is struck"},{"surface":"நுடங்கியாங்கு","parts":[{"text":"நுடங்கி","lemma":"நுடங்கு","gloss":"trembling"},{"text":"ஆங்கு","lemma":"ஆங்கு","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"just as it trembles"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"பகைஞர்","parts":[{"text":"பகைஞர்","lemma":"பகைஞர்","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கேட்டொறும்","parts":[{"text":"கேள்","lemma":"கேள்","gloss":"hear"},{"text":"தொறும்","lemma":"தொறும்","gloss":"every time"}],"gloss":"every time they hear"},{"surface":"நடுங்க","parts":[{"text":"நடுங்க","lemma":"நடுங்கு","gloss":"to tremble"}],"gloss":"to tremble"},{"surface":"ஏத்துவென்","parts":[{"text":"ஏத்து","lemma":"ஏத்து","gloss":"praise"},{"text":"வென்","lemma":"வென்","gloss":"I will (future first person singular)"}],"gloss":"I will praise"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வென்ற","parts":[{"text":"வென்ற","lemma":"வெல்","gloss":"victorious"}],"gloss":"victorious"},{"surface":"தேர்","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"chariot"},{"surface":"பிறர்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":"others"}],"gloss":"others"},{"surface":"வேத்தவை","parts":[{"text":"வேத்தவை","lemma":"வேத்தவை","gloss":"kings' courts"}],"gloss":"kings' courts","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"I indeed"}]}],"literal":"With ocean-like army and victorious plunder, / with thronged abundant strong effort, / the king of the cool Chola country, / with swaying mane and beautiful horses, / Nalankilli—we are bards who desire only him! / We do not want to receive gifts by singing of others; / we will sing of him, saying 'may his feet live!' / With ghee-seasoned meat and abounding / many rice with sweet tasty things, / from the hunger and suffering of great poverty, by your / previous days dismissed, the mature-wisdom children and / I, like the seven-gemmed beautiful-lustred beautiful hood-marked / eye-learning tasty-tongued / colored serpent, / our poverty having been removed, to give abundantly, / please send us away, O lord of swift horses! / Yours indeed is this wide world surrounded by the ocean, as everyone knows; / mine indeed is this great kinai drum with a clear drumhead like a cork-wood stick, / with a small stick containing fine rattling pebbles tied inside the drumhead, / which, every time it is struck, just as it trembles, your enemies / every time they hear it, to tremble, I will praise you / in the courts of other kings with victorious chariots!","translation":"O lord of swift horses, king of the cool Chola country, who possesses an ocean-like army, victorious plunder, and immense strength! We are bards who desire only you, Nalankilli. We do not wish to sing of others to receive gifts; we sing only of you, wishing long life to your feet. Having been fed by you in the past with ghee-seasoned meat, abundant rice, and sweet delicacies, my wise children and I were saved from the painful hunger of deep poverty. Like a serpent with a beautiful hood marked with seven gems, possessing keen sight and a sensitive tongue, we have shed our old skin of poverty. Now, please grant us gifts abundantly and let us depart. This wide world surrounded by the ocean knows that it belongs to you. As for me, my possession is this great kinai drum with a clear drumhead, beaten with a small stick containing rattling pebbles. Just as this drum trembles whenever it is struck, I will sing your praises in the courts of other kings with victorious chariots, making your enemies tremble every time they hear it!","modern":"கடல் போன்ற படையையும், போரில் வென்ற கொள்ளைப் பொருட்களையும், மிகுந்த வலிமையையும் உடைய குளிர்ந்த சோழ நாட்டின் மன்னனே! அசைந்து ஆடும் பிடரி மயிரைக் கொண்ட அழகிய குதிரைகளை உடைய நலங்கிள்ளியே! உன்னையே விரும்பும் பாணர்கள் நாங்கள். பிறரைப் பாடிப் பரிசில் பெற நாங்கள் விரும்ப மாட்டோம். 'அவன் திருவடிகள் வாழ்க!' என்று உன்னையே பாடுவோம். நெய் தாளித்த இறைச்சியையும், பலவகைச் சோற்றையும், இனிய சுவையுடைய உணவுகளையும் தந்து, எங்களின் கொடிய வறுமைத் துன்பத்தைப் போக்கி எங்களை முன்பு ஆதரித்தாய். அதனால், அறிவு முதிர்ந்த என் பிள்ளைகளும் நானும், ஏழு மணிகள் பதித்த அழகிய உத்தியையும், கூர்மையான பார்வையையும், சுவையறியும் நாவையும் உடைய பாம்பு தன் பழைய தோலை உரிப்பது போல, எங்கள் வறுமை நீங்கிப் புதுப்பொலிவு பெற்றோம். வேகமான குதிரைகளை உடைய வள்ளலே! நாங்கள் வறுமை நீங்கிப் பிறருக்குக் கொடுக்கும்படி எங்களுக்குப் பரிசில்களைத் தந்து விடை கொடுப்பாயாக! கடல் சூழ்ந்த இந்த அகன்ற உலகம் முழுவதும் உன்னுடையது என்பதை அனைவரும் அறிவர். என்னுடையதோ, கிச்சிலி மரக் குச்சி போன்ற தெளிவான வாரைக் கொண்ட பெரிய கிணைப் பறையாகும். அதன் உள்ளே கட்டப்பட்ட நுண்ணிய பரல்களைக் கொண்ட சிறு குச்சியால் அதனை அடிக்கும்போதெல்லாம் அது நடுங்குவது போல, உன்னுடைய பகைவர்கள் கேட்கும்போதெல்லாம் நடுங்கும்படி, வெற்றித் தேர்களை உடைய பிற மன்னர்களின் அவைகளிலே உன்னைப் புகழ்ந்து பாடுவேன்!","explanation":"The poet Kovur Kizhar praises the Chola king Nalankilli in this Purananuru poem belonging to the Patan tinai (theme of praising a king's greatness and asking for gifts). The poet declares that he and his family of bards desire only Nalankilli and refuse to sing of other patrons. He describes how the king's past generosity of rich, seasoned food saved his wise children and himself from the clutches of severe poverty, comparing their transformation to a serpent shedding its skin and revealing its bright, gem-like hood. The poet asks the king for abundant gifts so that they may depart and even share their wealth with others. He proudly states that while the entire ocean-girt world belongs to the king, his own possession is his kinai drum. He promises to play this drum and sing Nalankilli's praises in the courts of rival kings, making the enemies tremble with fear every time they hear of the Chola king's might.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.58],[1.58,1.95],[1.95,2.5],[2.5,2.9],[2.9,3.7],[3.7,3.9],[3.9,4.1],[4.1,4.7],[4.7,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,5.4],[5.4,5.7],[5.7,6.26],[6.26,7.1],[7.1,7.52],[7.52,7.7],[7.7,8.2],[8.3,8.48],[8.48,8.6],[8.6,9.3],[9.3,10.2],[10.2,10.7],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,11.4],[11.4,11.54],[11.54,11.6],[11.6,12.7],[12.7,13.1],[13.1,13.3],[13.3,13.6],[14.76,15.46],[15.56,15.76],[15.76,16.07],[16.14,16.26],[16.26,17.36],[17.36,17.65],[17.72,18.11],[18.17,18.36],[18.36,19.16],[19.16,19.56],[19.56,19.96],[19.96,20.06],[20.26,20.56],[20.56,21.46],[21.96,22.06],[22.19,22.33],[22.46,22.99],[23.06,24.06],[24.06,24.26],[24.26,24.86],[24.86,25.16],[25.26,25.56],[25.56,25.56],[25.56,25.89],[25.89,26.56],[26.56,27.26],[27.26,27.46],[27.46,27.66],[27.66,28.16],[28.16,28.46],[28.46,29.04],[29.16,29.56],[29.56,29.96],[29.96,30.06],[31.12,31.82],[31.82,31.92],[31.92,32.32],[32.32,32.92],[32.92,33.02],[33.02,33.52],[33.52,33.82],[33.82,34.57],[34.82,35.39],[35.51,35.62],[35.62,36.12],[36.12,36.12],[36.12,37.72],[37.72,37.72],[37.72,38.22],[38.22,38.32],[38.32,38.82],[38.82,39.28],[39.28,40.42],[40.5,40.82],[40.82,41.02],[41.02,41.32],[41.32,42.12],[42.12,42.32],[42.32,42.62],[42.62,43.92],[43.92,44.22],[4